{
  "statement": "Safety is paramount in ATM systems to ensure user trust and prevent financial loss. Requirements SAF-01 through SAF-07 establish a foundation for reliable operations, ensuring accounts cannot go negative, transactions are logged, and secure authentication is in place. SAF-06 provides safe degradation mechanisms during maintenance, which is crucial for user safety. However, I observe conflicts, particularly with EfficiencyAgent's requirements EFF-04 and EFF-05, which could prioritize speed over ensuring safety protocols are adhered to, potentially compromising user safety.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-04", "EFF-05"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "EFF-04 and EFF-05 may prioritize transaction speed and user delay reduction over the safety measures outlined in SAF-01 and SAF-03, leading to unsafe situations."
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
    {"id": "EFF-04", "stance": "oppose", "proposal": "Relax the requirement to allow for safety checks before confirming transactions."},
    {"id": "EFF-05", "stance": "oppose", "proposal": "Ensure that automatic withdrawals from the saving account are only processed after confirming sufficient funds."}
  ],
